published, so how

00:04:58.350 --> 00:05:01.480
should my code deal with
publishing exceptions?

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:04.470
And this happened when I
was moving topics around

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.740
and changing permissions.

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:09.560
TIANZI CAI: I'm glad you
asked about it because there

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:11.970
is something special here.

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:15.940
Most publishing failures
are retried automatically,

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:19.900
but in a case of non-retriable
errors, for example,

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:23.820
if the topic has been deleted
and you're using ordering,

00:05:23.820 --> 00:05:25.710
you shall call
out resume publish

00:05:25.710 --> 00:05:30.270
to restart published messages
of the affected ordering keys.

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:33.060
You can add this code
to resume the publisher

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:35.240
in a try-catch block.

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:37.960
MARTIN OMANDER: Hmm,
excellent, Tianzi, now,

